    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "William Clark Gable (February 1, 1901 – November 16, 1960) was an American film actor and military officer, often referred to as \"The King of Hollywood\" or just simply as \"The King\". Gable began his career as a stage actor and appeared as an extra in silent films between 1924 and 1926, and progressed to supporting roles with a few films for Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer in 1931. The next year, he landed his first leading Hollywood role and over the next three decades he became a leading man in more than 60 motion pictures.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999892615189,
      "temperature": 0.9999999892615189,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
